---

<Doc
  tocEntries={tocEntries}
  currentSlug="installing-plugins"
  title="Installing plugins"
  section="on-ramp"
  description="How to install a PlugDash plugin and where its settings live."
>
  <h2 id="two-kinds">Two kinds of plugin</h2>
  <p>
    readtime, tocgen and sharepost are render-time plugins. You install
    the package and use its component. There is nothing to register.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every other plugin has hooks, a block type or routes, so it is also
    registered in <code>astro.config.mjs</code>. Its options go in that
    call. The fromghost and fromsubstack docs cover the
    <code>@plugdash/import</code> CLI, which is not registered at all.
  </p>

  <h2 id="the-code-path">The code path</h2>
  <p>The worked example below uses <code>@plugdash/heartpost</code>.
  Every registered plugin follows this shape.</p>

  <h3 id="step-1-npm-install">Step 1: npm install</h3>
  <InstallCommand command="npm install @plugdash/heartpost" />

  <h3 id="step-2-register">Step 2: register in astro.config.mjs</h3>
  <p>
    Import the plugin at the top of the file, then add it to the
    <code>plugins</code> array of the <code>emdash()</code> integration,
    the one that sits inside Astro's top-level <code>integrations</code>
    array:
  </p>
  <Code language="js" filename="astro.config.mjs" code={`import { defineConfig } from "astro/config"
import emdash from "emdash/astro"
import { heartpostPlugin } from "@plugdash/heartpost"

export default defineConfig({
  integrations: [
    emdash({
      plugins: [
        heartpostPlugin({ collections: ["posts"] }),
      ],
    }),
  ],
})`} />
  <p>
    <code>emdash()</code> is an Astro integration, so it goes in Astro's
    <code>integrations</code> array. Each plugdash plugin goes inside
    <code>emdash()</code>'s own <code>plugins</code> array.
  </p>
  <p>
    The options object (here, <code>{`{ collections: ["posts"] }`}</code>)
    is the configuration. It is read from <code>astro.config.mjs</code>
    every time the site starts. To change it, edit the file and restart.
  </p>

  <h3 id="step-3-restart">Step 3: restart the dev server</h3>
  <p>
    EmDash reads the plugins array once at startup. Any change to it
    needs a restart.
  </p>

  <h2 id="admin-settings">Admin settings</h2>
  <p>
    Secrets are not put in <code>astro.config.mjs</code>. Two plugins
    take one in the EmDash admin, under <code>/_emdash/admin</code>,
    on the plugin's settings page:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>enrichkit</strong>: the AI provider API key</li>
    <li><strong>autobuild</strong>: the deploy hook URL</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Secret settings need the <code>EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>
    environment variable set in the server's process environment. A
    <code>.env</code> file alone did not work under <code>astro dev</code>.
    No other plugdash plugin has admin settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="add-the-component">Add the component to your theme</h2>
  <p>
    Add the companion Astro component to the relevant layout, usually
    the post page:
  </p>
  <Code language="astro" code={`---
import HeartButton from "@plugdash/heartpost/HeartButton.astro"
---
<HeartButton post={post} />`} />

  <h2 id="remove-a-plugin">Remove a plugin</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Remove the plugin from the <code>plugins</code> array in <code>astro.config.mjs</code>, if it is registered</li>
    <li>Remove any companion component imports from your layouts</li>
    <li>Run <code>npm uninstall @plugdash/[name]</code></li>
    <li>Restart the dev server</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Data the plugin stored stays in the database: KV values such as heart
    counts, redirects made by shortlink, SEO images made by socialcard.
    Delete them from the admin if you want a clean slate.
  </p>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nothing happened after publishing</strong>: hooks run on <code>content:afterPublish</code>. Saving a draft or an autosave does not run them. Publish the post (again, for posts that existed before the install).</li>
    <li><strong>Component renders nothing</strong>: for heartpost and shortlink, pass the post entry from <code>getEmDashEntry()</code>. The component reads the ULID from <code>post.data.id</code>; <code>post.id</code> is the slug.</li>
    <li><strong>Changes not picked up</strong>: restart the dev server. Plugin registration is read once at startup.</li>
    <li><strong>Plugin logs</strong>: in dev, plugin logs go to <code>.astro/dev.log</code>, not the terminal.</li>
  </ul>
</Doc>
